            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "@paligill@gmail.com I was thinking about the ApplyTime for VRs. In most cases, VRs should use `OnReset`, since applying updates `immediately` could trigger a power change in the system and potentially cause abnormal behavior. Instead of adding a new API to determine the supported ApplyTime based on VR type, we can simply define the ApplyTime for VRs as `OnReset`. Do u have any concerns?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com Please abandon this patch as you have  https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/+/83055 now."
                },
